Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:35.93,Title,,0,0,0,,ANI-DAX // REVIEW PROOF
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:35.93,Footer,,0,0,0,,Non-public FFmpeg proof render. Draft narration supplied for Daniel review.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.10,Body,,0,0,0,,What if Return by Death is not\NSubaru's advantage? What if it is\Nthe story's harshest interrogation\Nroom?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.10,0:00:13.04,Body,,0,0,0,,Most power systems reward control.\NReturn by Death removes control,\Nthen asks whether one person can\Ncarry memory, guilt, and\Nconsequence without becoming numb.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.04,0:00:20.73,Body,,0,0,0,,If Ani-Dax sat Subaru down after\Nanother reset, the first question\Nwould not be how many tries he\Ngets. It would be: what did the\Nlast version of you lose?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.73,0:00:29.40,Body,,0,0,0,,That is why the mechanic works. It\Nturns suspense into character\Nstudy. Every reset can move the\Nplot, but the real cost lands\Ninside Subaru before it lands on\Nthe timeline.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.40,0:00:35.93,Body,,0,0,0,,Ani-Dax takeaway: the ability is\Nnot interesting because it beats\Ndeath. It is interesting because\Nit makes survival emotionally\Nexpensive.
